Z||000005||saleenfiero||08-12-2001||01:14 PM||||The 93 mustangs were supposedly updated from 92 and their horserpower levels fell from 225('92) ro 205('93).  Torque fell 20lb ft.  The automatic stangs sucked without some work.  But if it was a 5 speed '93, their 0-60 is like 6.0 unmodified.  Good luck.  The 2000 stangs push 260 horses.  I'm just hoping to build a car to keep up with those.  They are fast.||||reg||1
Z||000006||My7Fieros||08-12-2001||11:48 PM||||My g/f was driving our 2001 Mustang V6 and I raced her in my 86 SE V6...I ran circles around her (and she can drive), she didnt have a chance....it was sad.(BTW both the Stang and the Fiero are manual trannies.)<BR>Then, I raced a friend of mine (in the same Fiero) against his 2001 Mustang GT...got my a$$ handed to me on a platter! Wasnt even close. To quote Clint Eastwood, " A mans got to know his limitations". Dont mess w/ newer model Mustang GTs in a stock Fiero.||||reg||1
